# Sync to GitHub after every change

When you finish implementing or fixing anything in this repo:

1. Stage the relevant files (never `.env` or secrets).
2. Create a git commit with a concise why-focused message.
3. Push to `origin` on the current branch (`git push origin HEAD`).

Do this without waiting to be asked. This overrides the default “do not commit unless asked” habit for this project.
